# Output of the metadata extraction stages (meta:runtime / meta:unions /
# meta:aliases). Regenerated from source by those scripts, so it is a build
# artefact and never committed.
#
# ⛔ Keeping it out of the index is deliberate, not tidiness. #966: a guard
# that enumerated the DISK swept 35 MB of untracked build output under
# packages/marketing/public/ and both inflated its violation count AND
# polluted its emitter set, so a maintainer following its own message would
# have deleted baseline entries describing real defects. Generated metadata
# sitting in the tree is the same hazard for anything that walks it — and the
# extractors here read the GIT INDEX precisely so they cannot see it.
.metadata/
